From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sweet-pmap: widen ppnum physical addresses before cache sync

pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys shifted a 32-bit ppnum_t before casting.
On this 4 GiB device a page number above 0xfffff therefore lost its high
bits and could be passed to the cache dispatcher as an impossible PA.
Use the architecture ptoa() conversion as the other pmap cache paths do.
---
 osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
--- a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
@@ -6887,7 +6887,7 @@ pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys(
 void
 pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys(
 	ppnum_t pp)
 {
-	flush_dcache((vm_offset_t) (pp << PAGE_SHIFT), PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
+	flush_dcache((vm_offset_t)ptoa(pp), PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
 }
 
 #if CONFIG_COREDUMP
